# spec-live overlay notes. NO BASE_SHA256 here, deliberately: like
# container/patches/boot-timing and draft-load-filter (and unlike
# qwen3.8-flash-next/patches/ple-ct-ignore) this NEVER replaces an upstream file.
# spec_live.pth is a new file mounted into site-packages; it installs a
# sys.meta_path hook that wraps/extends upstream objects post-import, looked up by
# name. If upstream renames or removes a target the hook no-ops and prints
# "[spec-live] NOT applied ..." -- the server then runs with its static draft depth,
# exactly as upstream does. Nothing to re-derive on snapshot bumps, but re-grep the
# names below on each repin (repin.md section 4).
#
# What it does: lets the MTP draft depth change on a running server
# (GET/POST /spec_tokens) by feeding vLLM's Dynamic SD (vllm#32374) a mutable K.
# The scheduler already picks K per step below num_speculative_tokens, the V2
# worker obeys scheduler_output.num_spec_tokens_to_schedule, and every allocation
# is sized for the maximum -- so the patch only replaces the batch-size lookup
# with one live value and adds the control path.
#
# Verified at vLLM 187a0eb (2026-10-10), by reading the source, by the host test
# (test_spec_live.py: fakes shaped like these seams), and by importing the three
# targets with the hook in a throwaway container of the b6d8e8a image (no GPU):
# all three hooks applied, EngineCoreProc._convert_msgspec_args passes the int
# through, and the real FastAPI resolves the routes with the right status codes.
# NOT verified: anything at runtime on the GPU (boot with Dynamic SD on MTP /
# hybrid GDN + QSA, K-specialised CUDA graphs, behaviour when K changes mid-run).
# Upstream documents Dynamic SD as tested with Eagle, Eagle-3 and DFlash only.
#
# Hook table (module -> attr):
#   vllm.v1.core.sched.scheduler          Scheduler.__init__ (wrapped; AsyncScheduler
#                                         calls super().__init__, so it is covered).
#                                         Reads self.dynamic_sd_lookup (list indexed by
#                                         batch size, scheduler.py:1485-1489) and
#                                         self.num_spec_tokens; swaps the list for a
#                                         subclass answering one live K.
#   vllm.v1.engine.core                   EngineCore: adds set_spec_tokens(k) /
#                                         get_spec_tokens(). Reached through the generic
#                                         utility RPC: EngineCoreProc dispatches UTILITY
#                                         requests with getattr(self, name) and the API
#                                         side calls engine_client.engine_core.
#                                         call_utility_async(name, *args) (same path as
#                                         reset_prefix_cache). They run on the engine
#                                         loop between steps.
#   vllm.entrypoints.launchers.api_server.routers
#                                         register_api_routers (wrapped): after the
#                                         original, app.include_router(GET/POST
#                                         /spec_tokens). Handlers read
#                                         request.app.state.engine_client.engine_core.
#
# Not hooked, relied on:
#   scheduler.py          num_spec_tokens_to_schedule goes into SchedulerOutput
#   gpu/model_runner.py   passes it to propose(num_speculative_tokens=...)
#   gpu/cudagraph_utils.py  captures K-specialised graphs for the K values in the
#                         BOOT schedule (num_speculative_tokens_per_batch_size);
#                         any other K falls back to PIECEWISE (dispatch())
#
# Caveats:
#   * Enabling it turns on Dynamic SD, which also stops the scheduler padding new
#     decode requests to 1+K tokens (scheduler.py:1124) -- a full-CUDA-graph
#     optimisation, not a correctness matter.
#   * The /spec_tokens route is unauthenticated (like every non-/v1 route here).
#   * K=0 turns drafting off for new steps (the MTP weights stay resident).
#
# Drift signals, printed to the container log:
#   "NOT applied: ... not running Dynamic SD"   the boot schedule was not passed
#   "NOT applied: ... not found"                a hooked name vanished upstream
#   "registered GET/POST /spec_tokens"          route attached (API server process)
#   "live draft depth on: K=<k> (max <m>)"      scheduler hook active (EngineCore)
#   "draft depth <a> -> <b> (max <m>)"          each change
#
# Drift check (host, stdlib only):
#   python3 container/patches/spec-live/test_spec_live.py
